(ned -- StartA, the whole A step, operator spec 2026-08-03.)
(  1. cal_a_zero  -- wall touches at -30 and -65, correct A, touch again.)
(                    It ABORTS if its own delta got worse, so reaching)
(                    step 2 already means the correction improved things.)
(  2. cal_probe_center -- re-find the puck. Rotating A SWINGS THE TOOL TIP,)
(                    so the centre and top measured before the correction no)
(                    longer describe where this tip touches. Re-finding makes)
(                    the stored zero correspond to the CORRECTED A.)
(The GUI then reads #3050 vs #3051 and writes head_zero.inc if it improved.)

(cal_a_zero parks at the puck centre, tip 5 mm up, which is exactly where)
(cal_probe_center wants to start its down-probe -- no repositioning needed.)

o<cal_a_cycle> sub
  #<cx>  = #1
  #<cy>  = #2
  #<top> = #3

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, StartA: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, StartA: no puck centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif

  (#3071 is the COMPLETION MARKER. The GUI must not decide "finished" from)
  (interp going idle -- that reads true momentarily BETWEEN the queued calls)
  (inside this cycle, and on 2026-08-03 it fired mid-run and auto-wrote)
  (head_zero.inc off a measurement that had not been taken. Only the last)
  (line of this file sets it.)
  #3071 = 0

  (--- 1: measure and correct A ---)
  o<cal_a_zero> call [#<cx>] [#<cy>] [#<top>]

  (--- 2: re-find the puck ONLY if A actually moved --------------------)
  (Rotating A swings the tool tip, so a KEPT correction invalidates the)
  (stored centre. A DISCARDED one does not: A is back where it started and)
  (nothing about the geometry changed, so re-probing would only cost time)
  (and put another set of touches on the puck -- operator 2026-08-03.)
  o20 if [#3072 EQ 1]
    (PRINT, StartA: A corrected by #3052 deg, dY #3050 -> #3051. Re-finding the puck so the zero matches the new A.)
    o<cal_probe_center> call
  o20 else
    (PRINT, StartA: correction discarded, A unchanged - skipping the puck re-find, the stored centre is still valid.)
  o20 endif

  #3071 = 1
  (PRINT, StartA DONE: dY #3050 -> #3051, A total #3069 deg, new centre #3045 #3046 top #3047)
  (DEBUG, StartA done: dY #3050 to #3051, new centre #3045 #3046 top #3047)

o<cal_a_cycle> endsub

M2 (end program)
